# IN-APP-IME-001 phase 2 — controller gate battery (run 104, 2026-11-21)

Run 103 died at 80/80 with the Rust half written but uncommitted. Run 104
(controller takeover) reviewed that tree, fixed two real defects in it,
wrote the full TS half, and ran the lane battery below. No gate output is
quoted from run 103 — everything here was re-run by the controller.

## Controller fixes on top of run 103's tree

1. `crates/langpack/tests/input_methods.rs` — the `set_capabilities`
   helper's `trim_start()` on the `license:` tail deleted the block's
   indentation, producing invalid YAML; 2 of 3 tests failed with
   `parse_error / manifest_missing`. Fixed by preserving the tail verbatim
   (`{head}capabilities:\n{caps}license:{tail}`). Gate-integrity note:
   this fixes a broken FIXTURE HELPER, not an assertion — the three
   assertions (absent→None, present→id:bool, malformed→schema error) are
   exactly as run 103 wrote them.
2. `apps/desktop/src-tauri/src/lib.rs` — new candidate tests use
   `OpenOptions … .write_all(..)` without `use std::io::Write` in the
   tests module: E0599, the whole lib-test target failed to compile.
   Import added.
3. `cargo fmt` re-run over the touched Rust files (run 103's tree was
   fmt-dirty: the fixed helper collapses).

