## TS half added by run 104 (contract in state/notes/IN-APP-IME-001.md)

- `ime.ts`: `InputMethodGate` + `inputMethodAllowed` (absent map = current
  behavior; present map = allowlist); `inAppKeyboardForScripts` and
  `packDeclaresInAppKanaKeyboard` honor the gate.
- `ime-candidates.ts` (new): `ImeCandidate` wire mirror +
  `LEXICON_CANDIDATES_METHOD_ID` + provenance label.
- `kana-ime.tsx`: `useKanaIME({candidates})` — Enter arms conversion for
  the trailing kana run (async lookup, stale/failed lookups never arm),
  SPACE cycles candidates and back, any other key / external edit /
  Escape disarms; `conversionLabel()` exposes provenance.
- `language.tsx`: InstalledPack gains `input_methods` +
  `input_methods_declared` (mirror of the Rust wire fields).
- `App.tsx`: gate threaded into keyboard resolution and the settings
  grant; `imeCandidates` callback gated on `lexicon-candidates` before
  the engine command is ever called; passed to the kana-input fields
  (writing, dictation target, my-words surface/reading, practice runner).
- `writing.tsx` / `practice.tsx` / `dictation.tsx` / `words.tsx`: optional
  `imeCandidates` prop forwarded to `useKanaIME`.
- Fixture hygiene: journeys harness + language/onboarding InstalledPack
  literals carry the tri-state fields (absent = current behavior).

